          "body": "Fixes #4\n\n## Problem\n\n`npx create-care-mfe-plug my-plug` generates a project without a `.gitignore`, even though `template/.gitignore` exists in this repo.\n\nTwo things cause it:\n\n1. npm never publishes files named `.gitignore` — it silently drops them (or renames them to `.npmignore`). This is long-standing npm behaviour and is why tools like `create-vite` ship their template gitignore as `_gitignore`.\n2. The package's own `.npmignore` has an unanchored `.gitignore` rule, which matches at any depth and so also excludes `template/.gitignore`.\n\nYou can confirm the published tarball has no gitignore at all:\n\n```\n$ npm pack create-care-mfe-plug@1.0.1 && tar -tzf create-care-mfe-plug-1.0.1.tgz | grep -i ignore\n(no output)\n```\n\n## Fix\n\n- Rename `template/.gitignore` → `template/_gitignore` (content unchanged).\n- In `initProject`, after copying the template, rename `_gitignore` → `.gitignore` in the generated project.\n- Anchor the `.git/` and `.gitignore` rules in `.npmignore` to the package root (`/.git/`, `/.gitignore`) so they only exclude the repo's own files.\n\n## Verification\n\nPacked this branch with `npm pack`, installed the tarball into a clean directory and ran the CLI:\n\n```\n$ tar -tzf create-care-mfe-plug-1.0.1.tgz | grep -i ignore\npackage/template/_gitignore\n\n$ echo 11110 | node node_modules/create-care-mfe-plug/bin/cli.js care_test_plug\n✅ Project created successfully!\n\n$ ls -a care_test_plug | grep '^[._]'\n.cursorrules\n.gitignore\n.husky\n.prettierrc.json\n```\n\n- `care_test_plug/.gitignore` is byte-identical to `template/_gitignore`\n- no stray `_gitignore` left in the generated project\n- also ran `node bin/cli.js MyPlugin` from source: `.gitignore` present, placeholders (`name`, `port`) still replaced correctly",
